stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Active
    Active --> Block: eligible idle or walk frontal melee
    Active --> LightDamage: accepted light hit
    Active --> HeavyDamage: accepted medium hit
    Active --> Knockdown: heavy or knockdown-flagged hit
    Active --> Dodge: eligible input / no committed attack recovery
    Dodge --> Active: committed dodge duration expires
    Dodge --> LightDamage: accepted light hit
    Dodge --> HeavyDamage: accepted medium hit
    Dodge --> Knockdown: accepted knockdown
    Block --> Active: animation completes
    Block --> LightDamage: accepted unblocked hit
    LightDamage --> Active: reaction finishes
    HeavyDamage --> Active: reaction finishes
    Knockdown --> GetUp: fall finishes and HP above zero
    GetUp --> Active: recovery completes
    Active --> Defeated: lethal hit / no auto-revive
    LightDamage --> Defeated: lethal hit
    HeavyDamage --> Defeated: lethal hit
    Knockdown --> Defeated: HP depleted
    Defeated --> DefeatedHold: fall completes
    DefeatedHold --> Respawn: revive or return-to-city transaction
    Respawn --> Active: reset transient combat state
    note right of Active
        Includes locomotion and combo phases in companion diagrams.
        Damage cancels queued attacks, preparation and charge effects.
        Existing immunity and enemy exposure checks still apply.
        Guard eligibility is further restricted in the cross-state table.
    end note
